      "id": "p1",
      "text": "As the hidden catalyst of spring weather shifted the landscape, a sleight-of-hand in the statistics revealed itself: a quantified enforcement activity shift saw apprehensions climb from 6,598 in February to 8,268 in March along the southwest border. Yet the grand illusion of control holds—for now, with year-to-date crossings remaining near multi-decade lows under asylum shutdown and deportation policies. Meanwhile, the hidden lever of funding stays jammed, as legislative decision-makers remain deadlocked over separate funding for immigration enforcement agencies in a pending reconciliation package.",
